export const CONCIERGE_DASHBOARD_KNOWLEDGE = "# ChainMore Dashboard Knowledge\n\nSurface: signed-in merchants only.\n\nHow the merchant dashboard at `app.chainmore.io` works today. Use it to\nanswer \"how do I …\" and \"where do I find …\" questions. Describe only what is\nwritten here. If a feature is not listed, say it is not in the dashboard and\npoint to `support@chainmore.io`. Never promise a feature, a date or a change.\n\nThe signed-in person's role and the account mode come with each question. A\npage or button that their role does not have: say so plainly and name who can\ndo it (usually the account owner or an admin). Do not walk them through steps\nthey cannot take.\n\n## Navigation\n\nThe left menu, in English and German. Pages a role cannot open are hidden.\n\n| Page (EN / DE) | Roles that see it |\n|---|---|\n| Overview / Übersicht | all |\n| Status / Status | all |\n| Notifications / Benachrichtigungen | all |\n| Onboarding / Onboarding | owner, admin, developer, support |\n| Payments / Zahlungen | all |\n| Customers / Kunden | owner, admin, finance, support, viewer |\n| Payment lookup / Zahlung suchen | all |\n| Sessions / Sessions | all |\n| API keys / API-Keys | owner, admin, developer |\n| Payout targets / Auszahlungsziele | owner, admin, finance |\n| Webhooks / Webhooks | owner, admin, developer |\n| Deliveries / Auslieferungen | owner, admin, developer, support |\n| Team / Team | owner, admin, support |\n| Billing / Abrechnung | owner, admin, finance, viewer |\n| Audit log / Audit-Log | all |\n| Integration / Integration | owner, admin, developer |\n| Settings / Einstellungen | owner, admin |\n\nRoles: owner, admin, developer, finance, support, viewer. Someone who opens a\npage their role cannot use sees \"This page is not available for your role\".\n\n## Test and live mode\n\n- There is no test/live switch in the dashboard. ChainMore sets the mode.\n  Before approval everything is test mode; after ChainMore approves the\n  account, the dashboard shows live data.\n- After approval the dashboard shows live keys, webhooks and payments only.\n  Test data stays separate and is no longer shown.\n- A banner on every page shows the mode. Test mode: wallet payments can still\n  move real money.\n- Payments, sessions, API keys, webhooks, deliveries, payout targets, exports\n  and notification settings are separate per mode. Team and audit log are\n  shared.\n\n## Top bar\n\n- Language: the EN/DE switch at the top. The choice is remembered in the\n  browser.\n- Light or dark: the moon or sun button at the top. Dark is the default.\n- User menu: shows the e-mail. \"Profile\" and \"Preferences\" both open Settings,\n  which only owners and admins can use.\n- Sign out: user menu, \"Sign out\", then \"Sign out now\". This also ends the\n  login; the next sign-in asks for the password again. There is no \"sign out\n  on all devices\".\n\n## Payments\n\nPayments / Zahlungen:\n\n- Newest first, 50 per page, \"Load more\". Columns: order / payment ID,\n  amount, status, mode, checkout, created, updated.\n- Find a payment: enter the exact `merchant_order_id` or payment ID in\n  \"Reference\", optionally a status and \"Created from\" / \"Created to\" (UTC\n  days), then \"Apply filters\". The search needs the exact value; it does not\n  find parts of a reference, amounts, wallets or names.\n- Click a row for the details: IDs, status, mode, requested amount, the asset\n  it settles in, times, transaction hashes of on-chain steps, and a timeline\n  from \"Payment created\" to \"Settlement recorded\" with \"Open evidence\".\n- Refunds and cancellations are not possible in the dashboard. Contact\n  `support@chainmore.io` with the payment ID.\n\nPayment lookup / Zahlung suchen:\n\n- Search by `merchant_order_id`, `customer_reference` or payment ID, exact\n  match. Shows the route, the amounts at each step, and the evidence page\n  with block explorer links.\n- \"Settled totals\" for a date range of at most 32 days (default last 30):\n  payments, settled, gross USDC, your net, fees, exceptions, on-chain check.\n\nUnder review: payments that are still not finished after about 10 minutes\nappear on a list reached from Overview or Status (\"Open review queue\"). There\nis nothing to do there except open the payment; if one stays stuck, email\nsupport with the payment ID.\n\nSessions / Sessions: these are the customers' checkout sessions, not login\nsessions. Search and filter work on the rows already loaded; use \"Load more\"\nbefore concluding a session is missing.\n\nCustomers / Kunden: enter the exact `customer_reference` your integration sent\nto see that customer's payments and totals. There is no search by name,\ne-mail or wallet.\n\n## Exports for accounting\n\n- Where: Payments page. Roles: owner, admin, developer, finance.\n- \"Export CSV\": downloads the currently filtered list, up to 5,000 rows.\n  Columns: `payment_id`, `merchant_order_id`, `environment`,\n  `requested_amount_minor`, `requested_currency`, `canonical_asset`,\n  `public_status`, `checkout_required`, `mode`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.\n- The export holds requested amounts and status only. It has no fees, no net\n  amount, no settled amount and no transaction hashes. For fees and net per\n  period, use Billing or the \"Settled totals\" on Payment lookup.\n- \"Large exports\" (CSV or JSONL) need both dates and at most 32 days. If a\n  large export stays \"Queued\" for more than 30 minutes, use \"Export CSV\" in\n  smaller date ranges and tell `support@chainmore.io`.\n- There are no invoices, tax documents, settlement or payout exports.\n\n## Billing\n\nBilling / Abrechnung shows settled totals and ChainMore fees for a period of\nat most 32 days. It is an overview, not an invoice. Some payment types have no\nUSDC value there, so \"Your net\" can read \"Not available\".\n\n## API keys\n\nAPI keys / API-Keys (owner, admin, developer):\n\n- \"Create key\", give it a name, \"Create\". The key is shown once; save it,\n  then \"I've saved it\". Test keys start with `cm_test_`, live keys with\n  `cm_live_`. The mode is set by ChainMore.\n- \"Rotate\" makes a new key and switches the old one off at once. There is no\n  overlap; update your server first.\n- \"Revoke\" switches a key off for good.\n- The list shows name, prefix, status, mode and created date. It does not\n  show when a key was last used.\n\n## Payout targets\n\nPayout targets / Auszahlungsziele: where ChainMore pays out. Without a target\nthe checkout offers no payment method.\n\n- \"Add target\": enter the receiving address. ChainMore suggests token and\n  network (a TRON address means USDT on Tron, a plain 0x address USDT on\n  Arbitrum). Networks: Ethereum, Arbitrum, Polygon, Optimism, BNB Smart Chain,\n  Base, Tron. Tokens: USDT and USDC. Then \"Confirm target\".\n- Check the address twice. A payout to a wrong address cannot be recovered.\n- \"Edit\" changes only the priority (lower wins). To use a new address for the\n  same token and network, add the target again; the new address replaces the\n  old one for new payments.\n- \"Disable\" stops a target for new payments. Payments already created keep\n  their address.\n- USDC targets are saved but not used for payouts yet.\n- Changing payout targets is limited to a few roles. Anyone else should ask\n  the account owner or an admin.\n\n## Webhooks and deliveries\n\nWebhooks (owner, admin, developer):\n\n- \"Add endpoint\": a public HTTPS URL; events as a comma-separated list, empty\n  means all events. The signing secret `whsec_…` is shown once.\n- \"Edit\" changes URL, events and the \"Active\" switch. Endpoints cannot be\n  deleted; switch them off instead.\n- \"Rotate secret\": the new secret is shown once. For 14 days each delivery\n  also carries a signature with the old secret in\n  `X-ChainMore-Signature-Previous`. A banner reminds you after 90 days.\n- \"Test\" sends a signed test event with `\"test_event\": true`. It needs an\n  active endpoint.\n\nDeliveries / Auslieferungen (owner, admin, developer, support):\n\n- Every delivery with status, attempts, last error and time.\n- \"Replay\" sends the same event again with a new `event_id`, signed with the\n  current secret. Owner, admin and developer can replay; support can only\n  look. Test events cannot be replayed; send a new test event instead.\n\n## Team\n\nTeam (owner, admin; support can view):\n\n1. \"Invite a teammate\": enter the e-mail and a role (admin, developer,\n   finance, support or viewer), then \"Create invitation\". Owners cannot be\n   invited.\n2. No e-mail is sent. Tell the person yourself.\n3. The person signs in at `app.chainmore.io` with exactly that e-mail address.\n   They need a ChainMore login first; if they do not have one, email\n   `support@chainmore.io` with their address. On their first sign-in they\n   join with the invited role.\n4. An invitation expires after 14 days. An expired invitation cannot be\n   renewed in the dashboard; contact support.\n5. One person can belong to only one merchant account.\n\n- Change a role: pick it in the member's row, \"Save role\". You cannot change\n  your own role or an owner's.\n- Remove someone: \"Remove access\", then confirm. Owners cannot be removed;\n  ownership cannot be transferred in the dashboard.\n- \"Revoke\" withdraws a pending invitation.\n\n## Account and settings\n\n- Onboarding / Onboarding: the setup checklist, the business profile and the\n  live access status. Owners and admins submit or update the business profile.\n  Live access is approved by ChainMore after review; it cannot be switched on\n  in the dashboard.\n- Settings / Einstellungen (owner, admin): account overview, business profile,\n  display name (\"Save display name\"). Legal name, currency and account status\n  change only through `support@chainmore.io` with the merchant ID.\n- Notifications / Benachrichtigungen: choose which alerts show in the\n  dashboard; owners and admins save them. Alerts are not sent by e-mail,\n  Slack or pager.\n- Status / Status: your account's open items (payments under review, failed\n  deliveries). It is not ChainMore's system status.\n- Audit log / Audit-Log: who did what in the account, read-only, no filter or\n  export.\n- Password and sign-in: the dashboard has no password, two-factor or\n  session settings. For sign-in problems, email `support@chainmore.io`.\n\n## What the Concierge cannot do\n\nThe Concierge only explains. It cannot see or change the merchant's account,\npayments, keys, payout targets, team or settings, and it never asks for\npasswords, API keys or secrets.\n";
